# Subnetting Notes

## Key Ideas
- An IPv4 address is 32 bits, split into 4 octets
- The subnet mask shows which part is the network and which is the host
- /24 = 255.255.255.0 = 256 addresses, 254 usable hosts

## Formulas
- Usable hosts = 2^(host bits) - 2
- Number of subnets = 2^(borrowed bits)

